y generated, while DSTC2 is a real-world dialog state tracking challenge dataset. The text does not provide specific details regarding data licensing, consent, or privacy compliance for the DSTC2 data. The supplied evidence is insufficient to determine if the data usage complies with specific privacy regulations or licensing terms.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper header lists the authors (Minjoon Seo, Sewon Min, Ali Farhadi, Hannaneh Hajishirzi) and their affiliations (University of Washington, Allen Institute for Artificial Intelligence, Seoul National University) along with their email addresses. The corpus build does not include a frozen venue/year anonymity policy to determine if this disclosure constitutes a violation of double-blind review rules. Therefore, no policy violation or compliance clearance can be declared based on the supplied evidence.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper cites relevant prior work and presents a novel model architecture. The corpus build does not provide frozen plagiarism-overlap evidence or information regarding parallel submissions. The absence of evidence in the supplied text does not prove originality or the absence of dual submission. The supplied evidence is insufficient to make a judgment on plagiarism or dual submission.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not contain a broader impact statement, a required checklist, or explicit documentation of IRB/ethics approvals. The corpus build does not include a frozen policy obligation that would mandate these specific documents for this submission. Without a corresponding frozen policy, no requirement for a broader-impact statement or other compliance documentation can be manufactured. The supplied evidence is insufficient to determine policy compliance regarding broader impact.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_R